            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a fragrance, then the Tamil for a cucumber."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: அஞ்சல் தலை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அஞ்சல் தலை — añcal talai — \"a postage stamp\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அஞ்சல் தலை (añcal talai) is native: añcal, \"letter post\" (DEDR 54), and talai, \"head\" (DEDR 3103). Early stamps carried the ruler's head, so a stamp became \"the post head\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
